  "unit_and_direction_caveats": [
    "BloodPressure is DIASTOLIC in Healthcare-Diabetes.csv but SYSTOLIC in heart_disease_uci.csv. They are used for DIFFERENT diseases (Diabetes vs HeartDisease) so they are never pooled together; a pooled 'BloodPressure' estimate would be invalid — keep the pairs separate.",
    "Glucose is fasting plasma glucose (Pima) vs avg_glucose_level (stroke cohort) — same unit (mg/dL) but different sampling; again only used for different diseases so no cross-unit pooling.",
    "Effect-size direction convention recommended: d = mean(cases) - mean(controls) so positive d = biomarker HIGHER in diseased group (expected sign for all 8 pairs).",
    "Rows with any missing biomarker must be dropped PER PAIR (pairwise deletion), not listwise across all biomarkers."
  ],
